OrchardLinux kernel (32-bit)
============================

The kernel Orchard runs on iPads with A5 to A6X chips (iPad 2, iPad 3, iPad
mini): upstream Linux v6.12 with the Apple 32-bit work on top. The A7 and
later boards are on branch main.

The branch is upstream plus one merge commit per layer: import/cascadia,
armv7/<subsystem>, configs. The work comes from Project Cascadia (rzxvx and
its contributors), Corellium's Project Sandcastle drivers as Cascadia ported
them, and Orchard's contributors; every commit keeps its author.

Contributing
------------

Kernel work for Orchard is a pull request here, against armv7; the orchard
repository (https://github.com/OrchardLinux/orchard) holds no kernel patches.
The checks compile the branch with orchard's recipe and run orchard's kernel
tests. Build your branch with:

    orchard build --device <board> --kernel-tree <dir>

Commit style: AGENTS.md. Orchard builds the commit named in its
kernel/upstream-armv7.lock; a pull request there takes a newer one.

Upstream's README: Documentation/admin-guide/README.rst.
